7b66","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"test/skill-parser.test.ts","size":5436,"sha256":"e8fb66c6b897d3e4bf356223aaad418bdca8ec7380d18ad2162ef15045b212dd","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"test/skill-validation.test.ts","size":23311,"sha256":"db2da59ef778605f2ce372c1b66652dc6ac73911d6107abdee843322773c3923","contentType":"video/mp2t"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2690,"sha256":"3b7b2417ac4f505feb840b563b9a8cc86dde8349f8259321c50239186b655c73","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789192005285,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"13bc2c3d03260f6bd3c49ff23039dbeb8339e9a7787b8fffc1ff0b5417c5277a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/13bc2c3d03260f6bd3c49ff23039dbeb8339e9a7787b8fffc1ff0b5417c5277a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780089943513},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":318,"checkedAt":1789192005285},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a powerful QA/browser automation toolkit, but it also handles real browser sessions and self-updates in ways that need careful review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The local browser daemon is purpose-aligned, but it stores persistent logs/state under .gstack, records full network URLs and console/dialog content, and exposes cookie-picker routes on localhost without the bearer token used for other commands.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Setup instructions invoke ./setup, but no setup or bin executables are present in the supplied artifact; the docs also recommend curl-to-bash Bun installation and upgrades from mutable origin/main or fresh GitHub clones, including auto-upgrade mode.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill directs broad future tool routing through gstack, includes fully automated ship workflows that commit/push/create PRs, and has cookie/session operations that exceed ordinary QA unless the user explicitly expects them.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persists browser sessions, cookies, update state, contributor reports, retrospectives, Greptile history, and optional global/project CLAUDE.md steering; these are disclosed but broad and durable.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The browser automation and QA workflows are coherent with the stated purpose, but the artifacts also include macOS Keychain-backed decryption/import of real browser cookies and a cookies command that returns full cookie values.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving this skill access to authenticated browser sessions and letting it persist local browser state/logs. Avoid importing production cookies, disable auto-upgrade, review any CLAUDE.md changes before accepting them, and do not run setup/upgrade commands unless you trust the upstream repository and have reviewed the exact code being executed.","findings":"[SDI-2] expected: Cookie import from real browsers is explicitly advertised for authenticated QA, but it is high-impact session access and the implementation decrypts browser cookies via Keychain.\n[PE3] expected: Keychain access is documented and uses fixed command arguments, but it still grants access to secrets needed to unlock real browser cookie stores.\n[T09] unexpected: The cookies command serializes full Playwright cookie objects, including values, while the architecture document claims values are only metadata/truncated.\n[T05] unexpected: The server deliberately bypasses bearer authentication for all /cookie-picker routes, including browser/domain enumeration and cookie import/remove operations.\n[T03] unexpected: Install and upgrade flows execute mutable or unaudited code: ./setup is missing from the artifact, Bun install is curl | bash, and upgrades reset/clone from current upstream before running setup.\n[T02] unexpected: README install instructions ask agents to add durable CLAUDE.md rules requiring gstack for all browsing and banning alternate browser tools, affecting future sessions and possibly teammates.\n[TM1] expected: Remove/reset commands are mostly install, uninstall, or development guidance, but git reset --hard and rm -rf are high-impact and should be treated as manual, reviewed operations.\n[TM2] expected: The chained project-install command is intended setup behavior but combines copy, deletion, cd, and execution in one pasteable line.\n[SC2] unexpected: The Bun installation advice executes a remote script without pinning or verification.\n[RA1] expected: The referenced self-modification concern is better understood as developer deployment documentation, not hidden runtime self-modification.\n[YR1] expected: The scanner's cookie-theft and destructive-action matches correspond to disclosed cookie import and maintenance commands, not evidence of malware by themselves.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789192005285}}}}}